Mission Local reported that all candidates supported bringing back street vendors. When pressed on how to protect them, Gutierrez and Bermudez proposed a committee or commission that included vendors; Hernandez called for a broad group of residents, merchants, vendors, cultural associations and city departments to devise a plan; Torres and Brown proposed designated vending spaces; and Fielder advocated for vendors’ voices and protection from criminalization.

